WEBVTT

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:47.140
Hey, here's an empty sack, and here's a list of what to put in it.

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:54.320
Buzzy, your list is just like a letter. It always starts out the same way.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:56.280
You mean the sort of deer, sir?

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:58.980
No, six plugs of chewing tobacco.

00:01:59.450 --> 00:01:59.970
Well, I got...

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:06.640
some kind of a stimulant don't I know you you're all buzzing but if those hills

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:10.190
come through with what I think they will we'll both have all the stimulant we want

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:17.350
and it won't be tobacco but what's that we'll expect you back you have the grub

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:19.420
ready by sundown I'll be back to help you

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:33.100
Do as I say, and nobody will get hurt.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:34.360
Drop or get your hands up.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:37.160
You passengers pile out of the coach.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:41.880
You Jets has got any shooting arms, throw them on the ground.

00:04:44.230 --> 00:04:47.180
Lefty, see what valuables our friends have got.

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:48.500
And be polite to the lady.

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:53.120
Turn around, I love you.

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:56.340
Now after your pocket's onto the ground.

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:07.010
Turn around. You wouldn't try that on me, now, would you, lady?

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:11.240
Sure a disappointment to me, ma'am.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:13.520
I sort of expected to find diamonds.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:29.420
Let me get that strong box.

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:50.520
We'll be right back.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:17.950
Here is Decker little iron box and plenty heavy get it out to my place you men split up. I'll see y'all later

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:36.120
What happened?

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:40.700
The date coat pulled up.

00:07:22.970 --> 00:07:26.610
one of your passengers no thanks pots the mail guard then it's held up the course and got away

00:07:26.610 --> 00:07:29.980
the strong box he's in a bad way but

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:30.700
I'm going to get him to a doctor.

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:31.760
All right, folks, give us a hand.

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:33.120
Yeah, let's see if we'll go.

00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:34.640
Take him up easy.

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:42.060
I'll drive back to Hagerstown.

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:45.360
I'll report to the sheriff as soon as I get to Temecula.

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:46.800
Have you ever been in Temecula?

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:47.120
Nope.

00:07:47.550 --> 00:07:49.610
Stranger around these parts, doing a little prospecting.

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:50.630
Why do you ask?

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:51.940
You'll find out.

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:54.860
There hasn't been a sheriff in Temecula since Britt Hodges was shot.

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:57.010
Stranger, that's one unlaw-abiding town.

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:59.890
Maybe so, but I need supplies and Hagerstown's too far.

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:01.780
Suit yourself and remember, I warned you.

00:08:42.350 --> 00:08:48.380
In that case, it's 500 pounds of sugar, and let me see.

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:56.780
Coffee, Dad, if you expect to sell all that milk and sugar.

00:08:58.100 --> 00:08:59.970
Almost forgot. Let us have...

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:14.920
five sacks of coffee green we do our own roasting lunch is ready wait on him i'm surprised to see

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:20.190
you i didn't think you'd risk a trip into our lawless town will you excuse me sam yes howdy

00:09:20.190 --> 00:09:25.020
miss jane your dad's just been telling me about the death of sheriff hodgins what's the matter

00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:29.910
with all the young fellas in temecula don't anybody want the sheriff's job or are they just plain

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:35.180
yellow it's getting worse each day it's nothing but a hangout for gunmen why even the stage line

00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:42.070
has left us off the route i'm sorry sam but we won't need those things dad ordered he doesn't

00:09:42.070 --> 00:09:46.980
know it but as soon as our supplies run out we're leaving here most of the other folks have left

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:47.340
already

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:25.660
be shooting up the town

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:33.690
Hey, let's get a couple of boxes, will you?

00:10:33.810 --> 00:10:34.110
Right.

00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:47.190
Here comes one of them.

00:10:48.340 --> 00:10:49.800
Let me handle it my way.

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:04.240
Give me three boxes of .45s.

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:05.170
We haven't any.

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:07.420
And even if we did, I wouldn't sell them to you.

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:09.860
Oh, a spunky little gal, eh?

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:12.380
I kind of like your type.

00:11:13.490 --> 00:11:14.330
Don't touch me.

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:17.060
Little spitfire, eh?

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:20.340
I'm asking you for those three boxes of ammunition.

00:11:20.560 --> 00:11:22.220
And I'm telling you they're not for sale.

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:23.890
Then I'm taking them.

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:27.160
Come in it.

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:29.960
What can I do?

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:33.080
Maybe I can do something for you.

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:34.460
You'll keep out of this.

00:11:35.310 --> 00:11:36.610
The lady's waiting on me.

00:11:36.810 --> 00:11:37.610
That's not true.

00:11:37.770 --> 00:11:40.450
I refused to sell this man ammunition, and he tried to take it.

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:41.530
Without paying for it?

00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:42.130
That's right.

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:45.870
Maybe that'll teach you to mind your own business.

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:48.340
Next time, you'll sell me what I asked for.

00:11:48.990 --> 00:11:50.170
That goes for you, too, Pop.

00:12:32.680 --> 00:12:33.840
Now, pay the lady what you owe.

00:12:42.760 --> 00:12:43.700
Take out what I owe you.

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:47.020
I told you that ammunition's not for sale.

00:12:47.810 --> 00:12:48.870
What's the matter with my money?

00:12:49.090 --> 00:12:49.790
Ain't it no good?

00:12:49.970 --> 00:12:50.950
You heard what the lady said?

00:12:51.230 --> 00:12:51.990
She's not selling.

00:12:52.210 --> 00:12:53.490
Now, pick up your money and get out of here.

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:08.140
Just a minute, mister. There's five more shells in this gun. You might need them.

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:20.720
I don't know how to thank you. Mister, uh...

00:13:20.720 --> 00:13:26.980
My friends call me Cheyenne. Did I see wrong, or did that left-handed fellow have three ladies' rings mixed up with that money?

00:13:27.880 --> 00:13:29.970
Did you see the miss... miss, uh...

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:36.720
Hilton, Jane Hilton. Yes, I saw the rings. One was a very pretty cameo. I'd recognize it again anywhere.

00:14:19.130 --> 00:14:21.600
a heap of money

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:23.070
that'd be enough to stake us

00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:25.760
by knowing something and proving it

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:26.660
that's two different things

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:33.240
Oh, Shy, uh, I've never been to Temecula, and there's nobody knows me there.

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:35.060
What's on your mind?

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:36.080
Oh, that water dough.

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:41.280
After you tell me about that umbri with the rings, well, things seem to drop right in your lap.

00:14:41.640 --> 00:14:43.720
Don't beat around the bush. You want to go out to the reward?

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:44.990
You're getting warm.

00:14:56.050 --> 00:14:58.950
Maybe it's that left-handed friend of yours coming to call on you with his friends.

00:14:59.240 --> 00:14:59.980
See what they want, fuck.

00:15:00.760 --> 00:15:29.340
taking them on one at a time but I don't like a gang up. I'd like to talk to Cheyenne.

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:35.380
Well, I'm Sheriff Rand from Hagerstown.

00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:38.900
I heard about the trouble you had in Hilton's store in Temecula.

00:15:39.400 --> 00:15:41.200
The nice job you did. Congratulations.

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:43.080
Well, Sheriff, I'd like to explain and...

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:44.380
Explain. There's nothing to explain.

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:45.760
But what I'm trying to say is...

00:15:45.760 --> 00:15:49.300
Now, listen. We need more two-fisted men like you in Temecula.

00:15:49.520 --> 00:15:52.540
Ah, shucks. I can't take credit from someone who really deserves it.

00:15:54.960 --> 00:15:57.720
Here's the most backward and unassuming gent I've ever met.

00:15:58.410 --> 00:15:59.970
I hope that when I'm shy and...

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:01.660
I'm as good a man as he is.

00:16:01.740 --> 00:16:02.820
You probably were, Sheriff.

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:03.840
You see, I'm Cheyenne.

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:06.740
Well, this other fellow, this.

00:16:06.880 --> 00:16:08.380
Hey, I resent that, Sheriff.

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:10.360
I tried to explain, you just out-talked me.

00:16:10.960 --> 00:16:12.720
You'll have to excuse my sidekick, Sheriff.

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:14.490
You see, he was acting on my orders.

00:16:14.970 --> 00:16:16.830
I wasn't taking any chances of a gang-up

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:18.350
from that left-handed gent and his pals.

00:16:18.510 --> 00:16:20.050
Well, that's what I call playing safe.

00:16:20.210 --> 00:16:20.630
Hey, Sheriff.

00:16:21.640 --> 00:16:22.180
Coffee's on.

00:16:22.970 --> 00:16:24.730
We got some beans and salt pork,

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:26.750
if the Sheriff and the boys could go for it.

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:28.330
Why, sure, where's my manners?

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:29.970
Oh, we wouldn't want to short you on your...

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:32.460
Sure, there's nothing. We got plenty of grub. Come on in.

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:34.700
Well, to tell you the truth, we could go for some coffee.

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:37.060
See, we've been riding since early this morning.

00:16:37.740 --> 00:16:40.070
Boys, loosen the cinches and come on in.

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:43.220
Break out the coffee, fuzzy.

00:16:43.460 --> 00:16:47.270
Now, when I was complimenting the wrong man a while back...

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:49.510
You mean when you was out talking, Nick?

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:54.810
I said Temecula could use a company of good two-fisted men, and I meant it.

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:56.920
What about good two-fisted men like yourself?

00:16:57.410 --> 00:16:59.410
Well, my star doesn't count Temecula.

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:02.280
You see, your cabin is right on the county line.

00:17:02.710 --> 00:17:04.170
That's where my authority ends.

00:17:38.860 --> 00:17:40.040
What do you figure is keeping lefty?

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:43.540
I think he's gone off his nut a little, from the licking he took.

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:44.710
So how do you figure that?

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:48.330
He rides the hills all day, trying to track down that stranger.

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:50.860
He's not tracking him because of the licking he got.

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:51.860
Then why?

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:55.080
Because he flashed those rings when he went to pay for the cartridges,

00:17:55.440 --> 00:17:56.580
and the stranger saw them.

00:18:03.870 --> 00:18:05.210
About time he was showing up.

00:18:21.310 --> 00:18:22.670
You don't look so good, Lefty.

00:18:23.550 --> 00:18:26.270
You wouldn't look so good either if you had the finger on you like it's on me.

00:18:26.780 --> 00:18:28.240
They got me tagged as left-handed.

00:18:28.440 --> 00:18:29.980
So what? They got me tagged as people?

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:32.610
It's only a moniker. You can change that any time.

00:18:33.050 --> 00:18:35.230
I was born left-handed, and you can't change that.

00:18:35.740 --> 00:18:38.140
Besides, that stranger knows I had the dame's rings.

00:18:38.970 --> 00:18:40.990
I'll get him. If it's the last thing I do, I'll get him.

00:18:41.030 --> 00:18:42.990
You listen to me. You're going crazy.

00:18:43.330 --> 00:18:45.050
You act like this is the first job we ever pull.

00:18:45.190 --> 00:18:46.310
Why we're all in this thing together.

00:18:46.910 --> 00:18:48.790
Now lay low and settle down for a while.

00:18:49.060 --> 00:18:49.900
You're just jumpy.

00:18:50.250 --> 00:18:52.170
I know what I'm going to do, and I ain't being stopped.

00:18:52.540 --> 00:18:53.420
I'll blast him.

00:18:57.840 --> 00:18:59.080
Get his neck in the noose.

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:02.920
too. Did you ever think what might happen if he gets tripped up?

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:59.610
store dad and his girl in hagerstown pardon me mister i didn't see you coming

00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:00.470
Oh

00:20:52.650 --> 00:20:58.910
old man Hilton had. I was in the Hilton store and saw him. The old man's going to drop the potatoes

00:20:58.910 --> 00:20:59.820
off at strangers.

00:21:00.220 --> 00:21:01.560
He's on his way to Hagerstown.

00:21:02.530 --> 00:21:03.390
What a break.

00:21:07.560 --> 00:21:08.220
A break?

00:22:05.140 --> 00:22:05.200
Thank you.

00:24:01.150 --> 00:24:02.610
It doesn't look as if there was anyone here.

00:24:02.950 --> 00:24:04.830
Well, I'll just leave the potatoes.

00:24:05.820 --> 00:24:06.580
Hello there!

00:24:20.000 --> 00:24:22.810
Oh, got your potatoes for you. Where do I put them?

00:24:23.090 --> 00:24:24.550
Well, inside the shack. I'll help you.

00:25:36.560 --> 00:25:36.880
missed

00:27:31.560 --> 00:27:33.710
All right, I'm coming out.

00:28:05.020 --> 00:28:05.780
A boudreau.

00:28:06.812 --> 00:28:08.132
That trick's as old as the hill.

00:28:09.084 --> 00:28:09.584
Fine, mister.

00:28:10.396 --> 00:28:11.036
Who are you?

00:29:03.804 --> 00:29:04.924
Can you beat that?

00:29:06.108 --> 00:29:08.128
The Hiltons are opening up the store.

00:29:10.012 --> 00:29:11.272
I told you Lefty was loco.

00:29:11.612 --> 00:29:13.472
I said if he ever got tripped up, things would happen.

00:29:13.820 --> 00:29:14.720
Well, things are happening.

00:29:15.292 --> 00:29:16.292
The Huttons are back.

00:29:16.444 --> 00:29:17.664
Lon Hart showed up yesterday.

00:29:18.492 --> 00:29:21.192
You just heard what Bart said about the Markham brothers reopening their place.

00:29:21.980 --> 00:29:23.320
What's the reason for the people coming back?

00:29:23.520 --> 00:29:24.940
Has the law come to Temecula?

00:29:25.080 --> 00:29:25.680
That's it.

00:29:25.980 --> 00:29:26.400
Wait a minute.

00:29:27.036 --> 00:29:28.216
Maybe that stranger.

00:30:03.260 --> 00:30:04.400
Can't you do anything but whittle?

00:30:05.820 --> 00:30:07.460
Can't that clock do anything but tick?

00:30:08.092 --> 00:30:10.932
Three days of wetland in Tekken. Not a word from anyone.

00:30:12.028 --> 00:30:13.028
Why don't you talk to me?

00:30:13.596 --> 00:30:14.596
Say something!

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:00.640
You can't go on.

00:32:00.860 --> 00:32:15.540
You're driving me crazy.

00:32:17.890 --> 00:32:18.950
I'll fix him!

00:32:40.350 --> 00:32:43.150
Thank you.

00:33:06.680 --> 00:33:08.480
Anybody own him?

00:33:11.080 --> 00:33:11.880
The one on the end.

00:33:13.080 --> 00:33:14.320
Well, that's Lefty's horse.

00:33:14.440 --> 00:33:16.200
Sure is, but where's Lefty?

00:33:24.090 --> 00:33:25.010
The road hard.

00:33:26.990 --> 00:33:28.310
Empty shell in the barrel.

00:33:44.710 --> 00:33:44.830
Who's that guy Jake?

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:02.700
He is in once before, he calls himself Fuzzy.

00:34:03.120 --> 00:34:05.160
Doing little prospecting up in the hills.

00:34:25.670 --> 00:34:26.430
Here comes Lefty.

00:34:27.740 --> 00:34:28.840
That's Lefty's horse, all right.

00:34:29.040 --> 00:34:29.940
That isn't Lefty right.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:31.330
That's Smitty.

00:34:40.290 --> 00:34:41.290
Where'd you get Lefty's horse?

00:34:41.430 --> 00:34:44.080
He showed up at the saloon, and Lefty wasn't on him.

00:34:44.300 --> 00:34:44.880
That's funny.

00:34:45.170 --> 00:34:46.150
What are you getting at, boss?

00:34:46.470 --> 00:34:47.750
Somebody could have trailed that Cayuse.

00:34:48.080 --> 00:34:51.400
Come to think of it, an old guy rode in right after we noticed the horse.

00:34:51.800 --> 00:34:53.640
Jake said he'd only been around once before.

00:34:55.170 --> 00:34:58.460
Lefty's horse shows with an empty saddle, and people are coming back to Temecula.

00:34:58.680 --> 00:34:59.960
Boys, it's time for a show.

00:35:00.030 --> 00:35:02.370
You, Bart, and Pee Wee, round up everybody.

00:35:02.740 --> 00:35:03.880
Tell Gun Hand I want to see him.

00:35:05.100 --> 00:35:05.280
Ready?

00:35:05.800 --> 00:35:06.600
I'll tell you what you're going to do.

00:35:30.920 --> 00:35:31.660
Still swarming?

00:35:33.590 --> 00:35:35.170
No, I ain't holding a thing against you.

00:35:35.950 --> 00:35:36.490
That's good.

00:35:37.960 --> 00:35:39.800
About those rings I showed back in Hilton's store.

00:35:41.200 --> 00:35:42.080
I came by them, honestly.

00:35:42.700 --> 00:35:44.160
Well, whether you did or whether you didn't,

00:35:44.420 --> 00:35:45.320
it's all the same to me.

00:35:46.970 --> 00:35:48.270
I suppose you'll be getting rid of them

00:35:48.270 --> 00:35:49.250
when you get to Temecula.

00:35:50.740 --> 00:35:52.980
Mister, are you telling me you're turning me loose?

00:35:53.140 --> 00:35:54.120
That's what I'm telling you.

00:36:10.720 --> 00:36:11.380
I'll go see my horse.

00:36:11.500 --> 00:36:13.500
Last I know, he was heading for Temecula.

00:36:14.020 --> 00:36:14.980
You cut him loose, remember?

00:36:16.630 --> 00:36:18.310
He probably made tracks for the hitching rack

00:36:18.310 --> 00:36:19.230
outside the saloon.

00:36:20.620 --> 00:36:22.940
Mister, it's a long walk from here to that saloon.

00:36:23.220 --> 00:36:25.400
Well, it's a nice day and it's a good road all the way.

00:36:25.640 --> 00:36:29.770
I'll see you again.

00:36:30.190 --> 00:36:57.770
So long travel with you that was right you're local you don't make sense why that's great you watch it

00:37:00.060 --> 00:37:01.000
Friends in Temecula.

00:37:01.560 --> 00:37:04.000
Maybe he's got friends in Temecula, too.

00:37:04.520 --> 00:37:07.000
Somebody shot out a rifle when you drew a beat on him.

00:37:08.080 --> 00:37:09.080
Who is the stranger?

00:37:10.070 --> 00:37:10.850
You don't know?

00:37:11.560 --> 00:37:12.360
Be smart.

00:37:13.400 --> 00:37:15.080
Don't go to Temecula.

00:37:31.920 --> 00:37:33.280
They're not safe across the line.

00:37:34.580 --> 00:37:36.950
They may pick you up over here.

00:37:38.480 --> 00:37:39.940
That'll not take any chances.

00:37:41.270 --> 00:37:42.410
Better head for the macular.

00:37:44.040 --> 00:37:45.400
You've got friends there too.

00:38:03.480 --> 00:38:08.430
If the law comes to Tamekna, those rings will hang you.

00:38:09.680 --> 00:38:11.180
Better get rid of them now.

00:38:34.030 --> 00:38:35.790
There, better.

00:38:35.990 --> 00:38:50.630
Or something.

00:38:51.600 --> 00:38:52.740
Must have a hole in your pocket.

00:38:53.720 --> 00:38:53.980
Maybe.

00:38:54.140 --> 00:38:54.620
Maybe not.

00:38:56.050 --> 00:38:56.650
No hole, mister.

00:38:56.890 --> 00:38:58.610
That money ain't mine, but these are.

00:40:04.640 --> 00:40:07.180
You all right, Lefty? I wondered what happened to you.

00:40:07.860 --> 00:40:08.900
You know where my horse is?

00:40:09.140 --> 00:40:10.860
Smitty rode him up to Decker's place.

00:40:11.660 --> 00:40:12.660
I'd better get it by myself.

00:40:12.940 --> 00:40:16.170
Wait a minute. You look as though you could stand a drink.

00:40:45.280 --> 00:40:49.870
Take the wire off that insulator.

00:40:56.770 --> 00:40:57.270
How's that?

00:40:57.390 --> 00:40:57.950
It's good.

00:41:20.730 --> 00:41:21.670
How do you know they're getting it?

00:41:21.730 --> 00:41:22.590
You haven't any receiver.

00:41:23.050 --> 00:41:25.110
I got the best receiver in the world, Matung.

00:41:26.640 --> 00:41:28.940
Put these wires in my mouth and I can taste the answer.

00:41:36.810 --> 00:41:42.180
I think you got it.

00:41:43.330 --> 00:41:44.710
No, I think you got it.

00:41:48.380 --> 00:41:49.680
Sure, now you know what to do.

00:41:49.860 --> 00:41:50.540
We understand.

00:41:51.480 --> 00:41:52.160
All right, let's go.

00:43:07.260 --> 00:43:17.400
Where have you been?

00:43:18.100 --> 00:43:19.040
Oh, hello, Decker.

00:43:19.400 --> 00:43:20.540
I asked you, where have you been?

00:43:20.740 --> 00:43:21.540
That ain't friendly.

00:43:21.820 --> 00:43:23.980
What happened to your shooting hand?

00:43:24.160 --> 00:43:25.460
I had an accident.

00:43:26.060 --> 00:43:27.680
Sure, when you were making your left-handed draw.

00:43:28.270 --> 00:43:29.590
You're wrong, Decker, so help me.

00:43:30.060 --> 00:43:31.720
Don't lie to me, you went gunning for that stranger.

00:43:31.940 --> 00:43:32.820
Did he beat you to the draw?

00:43:33.650 --> 00:43:35.070
I'll beat the truth out of you.

00:43:35.270 --> 00:43:35.730
Lay off.

00:43:36.230 --> 00:43:37.290
I don't feel so good.

00:43:37.450 --> 00:43:38.030
Let me alone.

00:43:38.550 --> 00:43:39.630
Talk, I'm listening.

00:43:41.030 --> 00:43:42.730
Like you said, the stranger beat me to the draw.

00:43:43.240 --> 00:43:44.040
How'd you find him?

00:43:44.570 --> 00:43:46.350
I trailed Hilton's wagon when they left town.

00:43:46.550 --> 00:43:48.270
I told him that Hilton was delivering

00:43:48.270 --> 00:43:49.930
a sack of potatoes to the stranger.

00:43:50.420 --> 00:43:52.080
And you're as dumb as Lefty's crazy.

00:43:52.200 --> 00:43:52.980
Why didn't you tell me?

00:43:53.380 --> 00:43:54.520
That ain't friendly, Ducker.

00:43:54.740 --> 00:43:56.640
And the stranger wasn't friendly when he plugged your hand.

00:43:57.040 --> 00:43:58.120
He was too friendly.

00:43:58.800 --> 00:43:59.980
He tended my hand and finished.

00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:01.580
and bedded me down until he turned me loose.

00:44:01.910 --> 00:44:03.170
So, he turned you loose.

00:44:03.270 --> 00:44:04.530
But your horse got here before you.

00:44:04.730 --> 00:44:05.710
Did he turn him loose, too?

00:44:06.050 --> 00:44:07.510
I lost my horse during the shooting.

00:44:07.750 --> 00:44:09.310
Another stranger trailed your horse here

00:44:09.310 --> 00:44:10.310
and maybe out to my place.

00:44:10.470 --> 00:44:11.570
No galoot with a beard.

00:44:12.200 --> 00:44:13.220
Whiskers knows you, too.

00:44:13.440 --> 00:44:13.980
How about it?

00:44:14.320 --> 00:44:15.200
Two of them work together.

00:44:15.360 --> 00:44:16.000
Where do they hang out?

00:44:16.350 --> 00:44:17.430
The old bonanza diggings.

00:44:17.990 --> 00:44:19.430
All right, boys, we're going to pay him a visit.

00:44:19.550 --> 00:44:19.890
Come on.

00:45:01.470 --> 00:45:02.410
and cleared out.

00:45:02.810 --> 00:45:03.030
Yeah.

00:45:06.470 --> 00:45:07.690
Now move closer to pay dirt.

00:45:07.830 --> 00:45:08.930
These diggings were just the beginning.

00:45:09.090 --> 00:45:09.950
You're welcome to the shack.

00:45:10.880 --> 00:45:11.780
They knew we'd come here.

00:45:11.960 --> 00:45:18.890
It may be a little rusty.

00:45:19.620 --> 00:45:20.680
I ain't had a checker game

00:45:20.680 --> 00:45:22.560
since Sheriff Hodgins passed on.

00:45:26.920 --> 00:45:28.260
Better keep your eye on the game.

00:45:36.400 --> 00:45:37.400
I guess I was wrong.

00:45:37.820 --> 00:45:38.980
Your mind ain't wondering.

00:45:40.480 --> 00:45:43.480
Hudgens fell for that play once and didn't talk to me for three days.

00:45:45.410 --> 00:45:47.900
Hey, Pop, take a look out the window.

00:45:48.740 --> 00:45:50.140
Do you know that fellow riding in front?

00:45:56.200 --> 00:45:56.920
Name's Decker.

00:45:57.670 --> 00:45:59.970
First time I've seen him in town for quite a sp...

00:46:01.760 --> 00:46:03.400
Cheyenne, come out here.

00:46:07.050 --> 00:46:08.150
Bracken just rode into town.

00:46:10.720 --> 00:46:12.200
And he's known as Decker here.

00:46:12.480 --> 00:46:14.980
Decker's the head of the gang that drove us out of Temecula.

00:46:15.240 --> 00:46:17.880
When I take dude Bracken, I'll relieve you folks of Decker, too.

00:46:31.690 --> 00:46:32.950
Well, your friends have cleared out.

00:46:35.010 --> 00:46:38.310
People coming back to Temecula and those two showing up here isn't just coincidence.

00:46:38.860 --> 00:46:40.540
There's one of them, boss, the old guy.

00:46:42.780 --> 00:46:43.940
Invite him over here for a drink.

00:46:52.260 --> 00:46:52.600
Join us?

00:46:54.580 --> 00:46:55.740
Well, I don't mind if I do.

00:46:57.040 --> 00:46:58.220
Sure nice weather for drinking.

00:47:03.740 --> 00:47:05.980
You know, this ginger beer is mighty invigorating.

00:47:06.550 --> 00:47:08.350
I hear you and your partner pulled up steaks.

00:47:08.640 --> 00:47:09.100
Yeah.

00:47:09.720 --> 00:47:11.940
Whoever said there's gold in them hills is crazy.

00:47:12.720 --> 00:47:15.100
You're figuring on leaving these parts, you and your partner?

00:47:15.940 --> 00:47:17.720
Well, kind of less.

00:47:18.240 --> 00:47:18.960
Kind of no.

00:47:19.260 --> 00:47:19.740
Depends.

00:47:20.100 --> 00:47:24.540
The place is kind of growing on me, and everybody's been so nice.

00:47:25.900 --> 00:47:27.600
Oh, order up another drink.

00:47:27.720 --> 00:47:28.560
This one's on me.

00:47:28.960 --> 00:47:29.980
You've had enough of that...

00:47:30.250 --> 00:47:32.380
What? From now on, everything's on me.

00:47:32.580 --> 00:47:33.400
I'm doing the ordering.

00:47:36.810 --> 00:47:37.410
Surprise me.

00:47:39.280 --> 00:47:42.060
Throwing away my ginger beer is right wasteful invigoration.

00:47:42.220 --> 00:47:43.620
And you're right wasteful of conversation.

00:47:43.840 --> 00:47:44.840
From now on, get to the point.

00:47:45.070 --> 00:47:46.650
Mister, where is your partner?

00:47:47.880 --> 00:47:49.320
Gosh, that's hard to say.

00:47:49.540 --> 00:47:51.090
Your scene ain't here.

00:47:51.350 --> 00:47:52.910
If you know what's good for you, you'll talk.

00:47:53.070 --> 00:47:53.650
I asked you.

00:47:53.790 --> 00:47:54.330
Where is he?

00:47:57.450 --> 00:47:59.070
Now everybody's been so friendly.

00:48:00.280 --> 00:48:02.240
All right, mister, have it your way.

00:48:03.160 --> 00:48:11.680
Keep it covered, buddy.

00:48:20.030 --> 00:48:21.850
Attacked you a long time, dude, Bracken.

00:48:22.690 --> 00:48:24.670
So, it was you all the time.

00:48:25.390 --> 00:48:26.890
I left you a note up the shack.

00:48:27.170 --> 00:48:29.320
It made you so sure I'd take you a visit there.

00:48:30.320 --> 00:48:32.800
Three rings, a sack of potatoes, and left his horse.

00:48:37.650 --> 00:48:38.950
One shot. That's the signal.

00:48:40.830 --> 00:48:41.630
That's the signal.

00:48:49.710 --> 00:48:51.050
You did me a favor, Cheyenne.

00:48:51.370 --> 00:48:52.410
That shot was a signal.

00:48:52.720 --> 00:48:54.080
That's my outfit out there in the street.

00:48:58.660 --> 00:48:59.980
That's right, dude. It was a signal.

00:49:04.250 --> 00:49:04.810
What's up, Decker?

00:49:04.970 --> 00:49:05.920
A hand. Get them up empty.

00:49:09.870 --> 00:49:11.290
They'll all be right in, boss.

00:49:25.010 --> 00:49:28.520
You ain't got no authority here. You're over the county line.

00:49:28.680 --> 00:49:29.220
You're wrong.

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:31.040
We've got plenty of authority.

00:49:31.620 --> 00:49:34.440
United States Marshal Cheyenne Davis made us as deputies.

00:49:35.060 --> 00:49:36.200
You're all under arrest.

00:50:03.230 --> 00:50:05.080
There's only one for you. Throw down your gun.

00:50:10.690 --> 00:50:12.480
Hey, did you get my telemogram?

00:50:12.960 --> 00:50:14.620
Sure. Didn't you get my answer?

00:50:15.560 --> 00:50:16.460
I'll say I did.

00:50:25.200 --> 00:50:26.060
Taking a hand in this.

00:50:26.360 --> 00:50:27.180
Stay out of there, Sheriff.

00:50:28.200 --> 00:50:29.360
That's Cheyenne's fight.

00:50:30.220 --> 00:50:31.660
And he wants to take him alive.

00:50:33.110 --> 00:50:34.230
I'll be right after you.

00:50:34.590 --> 00:50:41.680
I want to take you back to stand a fair trial.

00:50:42.500 --> 00:50:44.700
You'll have to show yourself to do that, Cheyenne.

00:50:44.860 --> 00:50:54.800
Your choice.

00:50:55.950 --> 00:50:56.830
I'm coming after you.

00:51:17.120 --> 00:51:23.300
You're left blamed for this. You put the Indian sign on us when you stole that woman's ring.

00:51:30.570 --> 00:51:31.770
Take them into the saloon, boys.

00:51:32.280 --> 00:51:33.980
That's the biggest place I know of to hold them.

00:51:49.060 --> 00:51:49.700
All right, Decker.

00:51:53.250 --> 00:51:54.170
Good work, Cheyenne.

00:51:54.510 --> 00:51:56.410
Thanks, folks, for coming back to Temecula.

00:51:56.760 --> 00:51:58.400
After that, nature just took its course.

00:51:58.580 --> 00:51:59.960
I suppose you'll be leaving Temecula.

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:01.260
now that your work is over.

00:52:02.800 --> 00:52:05.400
You know, I kind of like it here.
